# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Error mitigation and error suppression techniques are used to improve result quality when scaling up to larger workloads. This page provides high-level explanations of the error suppression and error mitigation techniques available with Qiskit.\n"
msgstr "Teknik mitigasi error dan supresi error digunakan untuk meningkatkan kualitas hasil saat memperbesar skala ke beban kerja yang lebih besar. Halaman ini memberikan penjelasan tingkat tinggi tentang teknik supresi error dan mitigasi error yang tersedia dengan Qiskit.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dynamical decoupling {#dynamical-decoupling}"
msgstr "Dynamical decoupling (dekopling dinamis) {#dynamical-decoupling}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum circuits are executed on IBM&reg; hardware as sequences of microwave pulses that need to be scheduled and run at precise time intervals.\n"
"Unfortunately, unwanted interactions between qubits can lead to coherent errors on idling qubits. Dynamical decoupling works by inserting pulse sequences on idling qubits to approximately cancel out the effect of these errors. Each inserted pulse sequence amounts to an identity operation, but the physical presence of the pulses has the effect of suppressing errors.\n"
"There are many possible choices of pulse sequences, and which sequence is better for each particular case remains an [active area of research](https://journals.aps.org/prapplied/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevApplied.20.064027).\n"
msgstr ""
"Circuit kuantum dieksekusi pada perangkat keras IBM&reg; sebagai rangkaian pulsa gelombang mikro yang perlu dijadwalkan dan dijalankan pada interval waktu yang tepat.\n"
"Sayangnya, interaksi yang tidak diinginkan antar qubit dapat menyebabkan error koheren pada qubit yang sedang diam. Dynamical decoupling bekerja dengan menyisipkan rangkaian pulsa pada qubit yang diam untuk secara aproksimatif meniadakan efek error tersebut. Setiap rangkaian pulsa yang disisipkan setara dengan operasi identitas, namun keberadaan fisik pulsa tersebut berfungsi untuk menekan error.\n"
"Ada banyak pilihan rangkaian pulsa, dan rangkaian mana yang lebih baik untuk setiap kasus tertentu masih menjadi [area penelitian aktif](https://journals.aps.org/prapplied/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevApplied.20.064027).\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-12 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that dynamical decoupling is mainly useful for circuits containing gaps in which some qubits sit idle without any operations acting on them. If the operations in the circuit are packed very densely, such that all of the qubits are busy most of the time, then the addition of dynamical decoupling pulses might not improve performance. In fact, it could even worsen performance due to imperfections in the pulses themselves.\n"
msgstr "Perlu dicatat bahwa dynamical decoupling terutama berguna untuk Circuit yang memiliki celah saat sebagian qubit menganggur tanpa ada operasi yang dikenakan padanya. Jika operasi dalam Circuit sangat padat, sehingga semua qubit sibuk sebagian besar waktu, maka penambahan pulsa dynamical decoupling mungkin tidak meningkatkan performa. Bahkan, hal itu bisa memperburuk performa karena ketidaksempurnaan pada pulsa itu sendiri.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The diagram below depicts dynamical decoupling with an XX pulse sequence. The abstract circuit on the left is mapped onto a microwave pulse schedule on the top right. The bottom right depicts the same schedule, but with a sequence of two X pulses inserted during an idle period of the first qubit.\n"
msgstr "Diagram di bawah ini menggambarkan dynamical decoupling dengan rangkaian pulsa XX. Circuit abstrak di sebelah kiri dipetakan ke jadwal pulsa gelombang mikro di kanan atas. Kanan bawah menggambarkan jadwal yang sama, namun dengan rangkaian dua pulsa X yang disisipkan selama periode diam qubit pertama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Depiction of dynamical decoupling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/dd.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Gambaran dynamical decoupling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/dd.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can enable dynamical decoupling the following ways:\n"
"    - The [Dynamical decoupling transpiler pass](/guides/dynamical-decoupling-pass-manager) in Qiskit\n"
"    - The dynamical decoupling option if using IBM Quantum [Estimator](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-estimator-options#dynamical_decoupling) or [Sampler](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-sampler-options#dynamical_decoupling)\n"
msgstr ""
"Kamu dapat mengaktifkan dynamical decoupling dengan cara berikut:\n"
"    - [Dynamical decoupling transpiler pass](/guides/dynamical-decoupling-pass-manager) di Qiskit\n"
"    - Opsi dynamical decoupling jika menggunakan IBM Quantum [Estimator](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-estimator-options#dynamical_decoupling) atau [Sampler](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-sampler-options#dynamical_decoupling)\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-09 · verified 2026-09-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling {#pauli-twirling}"
msgstr "Twirling Pauli {#pauli-twirling}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Twirling, also known as [randomized compiling](https://journals.aps.org/pra/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevA.94.052325), is a widely used technique for converting arbitrary noise channels into noise channels with more specific structure.\n"
msgstr "Twirling, juga dikenal sebagai [randomized compiling](https://journals.aps.org/pra/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevA.94.052325), adalah teknik yang banyak digunakan untuk mengubah kanal noise arbitrer menjadi kanal noise dengan struktur yang lebih spesifik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling is a special kind of twirling that uses Pauli operations. It has the effect of transforming any quantum channel into a Pauli channel. Performed alone, it can mitigate coherent noise because coherent noise tends to accumulate quadratically with the number of operations, whereas Pauli noise accumulates linearly. Pauli twirling is often combined with other error mitigation techniques that work better with Pauli noise than with arbitrary noise.\n"
msgstr "Pauli twirling adalah jenis twirling khusus yang menggunakan operasi Pauli. Teknik ini berfungsi untuk mengubah kanal kuantum apa pun menjadi kanal Pauli. Dilakukan sendiri, teknik ini dapat memitigasi noise koheren karena noise koheren cenderung terakumulasi secara kuadratik seiring jumlah operasi, sedangkan noise Pauli terakumulasi secara linier. Pauli twirling sering dikombinasikan dengan teknik mitigasi error lain yang bekerja lebih baik dengan noise Pauli daripada noise arbitrer.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling is implemented by sandwiching a chosen set of gates with randomly chosen single-qubit Pauli gates in such a way that the ideal effect of the gate remains the same. The result is that a single circuit is replaced with a random ensemble of circuits, all with the same ideal effect. When sampling the circuit, samples are drawn from multiple random instances, rather than just a single one.\n"
msgstr "Pauli twirling diimplementasikan dengan mengapit sekumpulan Gate yang dipilih dengan Gate Pauli satu qubit yang dipilih secara acak sedemikian rupa sehingga efek ideal dari Gate tetap sama. Hasilnya adalah satu Circuit digantikan dengan ansambel Circuit acak, semuanya dengan efek ideal yang sama. Saat mengambil sampel Circuit, sampel diambil dari beberapa instance acak, bukan hanya satu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Depiction of Pauli twirling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/pauli_twirling.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Gambaran Pauli twirling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/pauli_twirling.svg)\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-12 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since most of the errors in current quantum hardware come from two-qubit gates, this technique is often applied exclusively to (native) two-qubit gates. The following diagram depicts some Pauli twirls for the CNOT and ECR gates. Every circuit within a row has the same ideal effect.\n"
msgstr "Karena sebagian besar error pada perangkat keras kuantum saat ini berasal dari Gate dua qubit, teknik ini sering diterapkan secara eksklusif pada Gate dua qubit (asli). Diagram berikut menggambarkan beberapa Pauli twirl untuk Gate CNOT dan ECR. Setiap Circuit dalam satu baris memiliki efek ideal yang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Depiction of gate twirls](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/gate_twirls.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Gambaran twirl Gate](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/gate_twirls.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can enable Pauli twirling the following ways:\n"
"    - A [Pauli twirling custom pass](/guides/custom-transpiler-pass) in Qiskit\n"
"    - The twirling options if using IBM Quantum [Estimator](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-estimator-options#twirling) or [Sampler](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-sampler-options#twirling)\n"
msgstr ""
"Kamu dapat mengaktifkan Pauli twirling dengan cara berikut:\n"
"    - [Custom pass Pauli twirling](/guides/custom-transpiler-pass) di Qiskit\n"
"    - Opsi twirling jika menggunakan IBM Quantum [Estimator](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-estimator-options#twirling) atau [Sampler](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-sampler-options#twirling)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"trex\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"trex\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX) {#twirled-readout-error-extinction-trex}"
msgstr "Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX) {#twirled-readout-error-extinction-trex}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX)](https://journals.aps.org/pra/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevA.105.032620) mitigates the effect of measurement errors for the estimation of Pauli observable expectation values.\n"
"It is based on the notion of twirled measurements, which are accomplished by randomly substituting measurement gates by a sequence of (1) a Pauli X gate, (2) a measurement, and (3) classical bit flip. Just like in standard gate twirling, this sequence is equivalent to a plain measurement in the absence of noise, as depicted in the following diagram:\n"
msgstr ""
"[Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX)](https://journals.aps.org/pra/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevA.105.032620) memitigasi efek error pengukuran untuk estimasi nilai ekspektasi observabel Pauli.\n"
"Teknik ini didasarkan pada konsep twirled measurements, yang dilakukan dengan secara acak mengganti Gate pengukuran dengan rangkaian (1) Gate Pauli X, (2) pengukuran, dan (3) bit flip klasik. Sama seperti gate twirling standar, rangkaian ini setara dengan pengukuran biasa tanpa adanya noise, seperti yang digambarkan dalam diagram berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Depiction of measurement twirling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/measurement_twirling.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Gambaran measurement twirling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/measurement_twirling.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the presence of readout error, measurement twirling has the effect of diagonalizing the readout-error transfer matrix, making it easy to invert. A rescaling term from the diagonal noise channel is learned by\n"
"benchmarking random circuits initialized in the zero state. This allows\n"
"the service to remove bias from expectation values that result from\n"
"readout noise. Estimating the readout-error transfer matrix requires executing additional calibration circuits, which introduces a small overhead.\n"
msgstr "Dengan adanya readout error, measurement twirling berfungsi untuk mendiagonalisasi matriks transfer readout-error, sehingga mudah untuk diinversikan. Sebuah suku penskalaan ulang dari kanal noise diagonal dipelajari dengan melakukan benchmarking Circuit acak yang diinisialisasi dalam keadaan nol. Hal ini memungkinkan layanan untuk menghilangkan bias dari nilai ekspektasi yang dihasilkan oleh readout noise. Mengestimasi matriks transfer readout-error memerlukan eksekusi Circuit kalibrasi tambahan, yang menimbulkan sedikit overhead.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can enable TREX the following ways:\n"
"    - The [Qiskit Mitigation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-mitigation/trex#trex) addon for Qiskit\n"
"    - The [`measure_mitigation` option](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-resilience-options#measure_mitigation) if using IBM Quantum Estimator\n"
"    - The [resilience level](/guides/estimator-noise-management#resilience) if using IBM Quantum Estimator\n"
msgstr ""
"Kamu dapat mengaktifkan TREX dengan cara berikut:\n"
"    - Addon [Qiskit Mitigation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-mitigation/trex#trex) untuk Qiskit\n"
"    - [Opsi `measure_mitigation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-resilience-options#measure_mitigation) jika menggunakan IBM Quantum Estimator\n"
"    - [Tingkat resiliensi](/guides/estimator-noise-management#resilience) jika menggunakan IBM Quantum Estimator\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"zne\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"zne\"></span>\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-09 · verified 2026-09-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) {#zero-noise-extrapolation-zne}"
msgstr "Ekstrapolasi noise-nol (ZNE) {#zero-noise-extrapolation-zne}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) is a technique for mitigating errors in estimating expectation values of observables. While it often improves results, it is not guaranteed to produce an unbiased result.\n"
msgstr "Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) adalah teknik untuk memitigasi error dalam mengestimasi nilai ekspektasi observabel. Meskipun sering meningkatkan hasil, teknik ini tidak dijamin menghasilkan hasil yang tidak bias.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "ZNE consists of two stages:\n"
msgstr "ZNE terdiri dari dua tahap:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "_Noise amplification_: The original quantum circuit is executed multiple times at different noise rates.\n"
msgstr "_Amplifikasi noise_: Circuit kuantum asli dieksekusi beberapa kali pada tingkat noise yang berbeda.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "_Extrapolation_: The ideal result is estimated by extrapolating the noisy expectation value results to the zero-noise limit.\n"
msgstr "_Ekstrapolasi_: Hasil ideal diestimasi dengan mengekstrapolasi hasil nilai ekspektasi yang noisy ke batas zero-noise.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Both the noise amplification and extrapolation stages can be implemented in many different ways. IBM Quantum Compute implements noise amplification by \"digital gate folding,\" which means that two-qubit gates are replaced with equivalent sequences of the gate and its inverse. For example, replacing a unitary $U$ with $U U^\\dagger U$ would yield a noise amplification factor of 3. For the extrapolation, you can choose from one of several functional forms, including a linear fit or an exponential fit.\n"
"The image below depicts digital gate folding on the left, and the extrapolation procedure on the right.\n"
msgstr ""
"Baik tahap amplifikasi noise maupun ekstrapolasi dapat diimplementasikan dengan berbagai cara. IBM Quantum Compute mengimplementasikan amplifikasi noise dengan \"digital gate folding,\" yang berarti Gate dua qubit digantikan dengan rangkaian ekuivalen dari Gate dan inversnya. Misalnya, mengganti operator uniter $U$ dengan $U U^\\dagger U$ akan menghasilkan faktor amplifikasi noise sebesar 3. Untuk ekstrapolasi, kamu dapat memilih salah satu dari beberapa bentuk fungsional, termasuk fit linier atau fit eksponensial.\n"
"Gambar di bawah ini menggambarkan digital gate folding di sebelah kiri, dan prosedur ekstrapolasi di sebelah kanan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Depiction of ZNE](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/zne.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Gambaran ZNE](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/zne.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The overhead of this method scales with the number of noise factors. The\n"
"default settings sample the expectation value at three noise factors,\n"
"leading to a roughly 3x overhead.\n"
msgstr "Overhead dari metode ini berskala dengan jumlah faktor noise. Pengaturan default mengambil sampel nilai ekspektasi pada tiga faktor noise, sehingga menghasilkan overhead sekitar 3x.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can enable ZNE the following ways:\n"
"    - The [Qiskit Mitigation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-mitigation/zne) addon for Qiskit\n"
"    - The [`zne_mitigation` option](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-resilience-options#zne_mitigation) if using IBM Quantum Estimator\n"
"    - The [resilience level](/guides/estimator-noise-management#resilience) if using IBM Quantum Estimator\n"
msgstr ""
"Kamu dapat mengaktifkan ZNE dengan cara berikut:\n"
"    - Addon [Qiskit Mitigation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-mitigation/zne) untuk Qiskit\n"
"    - [Opsi `zne_mitigation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-resilience-options#zne_mitigation) jika menggunakan IBM Quantum Estimator\n"
"    - [Tingkat resiliensi](/guides/estimator-noise-management#resilience) jika menggunakan IBM Quantum Estimator\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"pea\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"pea\"></span>\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-09 · verified 2026-09-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilistic Error Amplification (PEA) {#probabilistic-error-amplification-pea}"
msgstr "Amplifikasi Error Probabilistik (PEA) {#probabilistic-error-amplification-pea}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One of the main challenges in ZNE is to accurately amplify the noise affecting the target circuit. Gate folding provides an easy way to perform this amplification, but is potentially inaccurate and might lead to incorrect results.  See the article [\"Scalable error mitigation for noisy quantum circuits produces competitive expectation values\"](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2108.09197), and specifically page 4 of the supplementary information for details. Probabilistic error amplification provides a more accurate approach to error amplification through noise learning.\n"
msgstr "Salah satu tantangan utama dalam ZNE adalah mengamplifikasi noise yang mempengaruhi Circuit target secara akurat. Gate folding menyediakan cara mudah untuk melakukan amplifikasi ini, namun berpotensi tidak akurat dan dapat menghasilkan hasil yang salah. Lihat artikel [\"Scalable error mitigation for noisy quantum circuits produces competitive expectation values\"](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2108.09197), khususnya halaman 4 dari informasi tambahan untuk detailnya. Probabilistic error amplification memberikan pendekatan yang lebih akurat untuk amplifikasi error melalui pembelajaran noise.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEA is a more sophisticated technique that performs preliminary experiments to reconstruct the noise and then uses this information to perform an accurate amplification. It starts by learning the twirled noise model of each layer of entangling gates in the circuit before they are run. After the learning phase, the circuits are executed at each noise factor, where every entangling layer of the circuits is amplified by probabilistically injecting single-qubit noise proportional to the corresponding learned noise model. See the article [\"Evidence for the utility of quantum computing before fault tolerance\"](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-023-06096-3) for more details.\n"
msgstr "PEA adalah teknik yang lebih canggih yang melakukan eksperimen pendahuluan untuk merekonstruksi noise dan kemudian menggunakan informasi ini untuk melakukan amplifikasi yang akurat. Teknik ini dimulai dengan mempelajari model noise yang di-twirl dari setiap lapisan Gate entangling dalam Circuit sebelum dijalankan. Setelah fase pembelajaran, Circuit dieksekusi pada setiap faktor noise, di mana setiap lapisan entangling dari Circuit diamplifikasi dengan menyuntikkan secara probabilistik noise satu qubit yang proporsional dengan model noise yang dipelajari dan bersesuaian untuk lapisan tersebut. Lihat artikel [\"Evidence for the utility of quantum computing before fault tolerance\"](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-023-06096-3) untuk detail lebih lanjut.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"PEA consists of three stages:\n"
"1. _Learning_: The twirled noise model of each layer of entangling gates in the circuit is learned.\n"
"1. _Noise amplification_: The original quantum circuit is executed multiple times at different noise factors.\n"
"2. _Extrapolation_: The ideal result is estimated by extrapolating the noisy expectation value results to the zero-noise limit.\n"
msgstr ""
"PEA terdiri dari tiga tahap:\n"
"1. _Pembelajaran_: Model noise yang di-twirl dari setiap lapisan Gate entangling dalam Circuit dipelajari.\n"
"1. _Amplifikasi noise_: Circuit kuantum asli dieksekusi beberapa kali pada faktor noise yang berbeda.\n"
"2. _Ekstrapolasi_: Hasil ideal diestimasi dengan mengekstrapolasi hasil nilai ekspektasi yang ber-noise ke batas zero-noise.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For utility-scale experiments, PEA is often the best choice.\n"
msgstr "Untuk eksperimen skala utilitas, PEA sering menjadi pilihan terbaik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because PEA is a ZNE noise amplification technique, you also need to enable ZNE. You can enable PEA and ZNE  the following ways:\n"
"    - The [Qiskit Mitigation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-mitigation/zne) addon for Qiskit\n"
"    - The [`zne_mitigation` option](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-resilience-options#zne_mitigation) with [`pea`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-zne-options#amplifier) as the amplifier if using IBM Quantum Estimator\n"
msgstr ""
"Karena PEA adalah teknik amplifikasi noise ZNE, kamu juga perlu mengaktifkan ZNE. Kamu dapat mengaktifkan PEA dan ZNE dengan cara berikut:\n"
"    - Addon [Qiskit Mitigation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-mitigation/zne) untuk Qiskit\n"
"    - [Opsi `zne_mitigation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-resilience-options#zne_mitigation) dengan [`pea`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-zne-options#amplifier) sebagai amplifier jika menggunakan IBM Quantum Estimator\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
